      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "A 19-year-old woman presented with frontal headaches, papilledema, and binocular horizontal double vision due to a left VI nerve palsy. MRV demonstrated sagittal sinus and bilateral transverse sinus thrombosis. The clinical and neuro-radiologic signs resolved after anticoagulation."},
